From ddc9daa6aaefb0ae459db80bfff5e5e1f78c46ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Johan (via Claude)" <[email protected]>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 21:42:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add direct-Moonraker mode (no Home Assistant required)

Adds an alternative to the Home Assistant + ha_creality_ws discovery/
automation path: connect straight to a printer's Moonraker API.

- lib/api/moonraker-direct.ts: queries box/print_stats directly, maps
  into the existing HAPrinter/HATray/HAAMS shapes so nothing downstream
  needed to change.
- lib/direct-poller.ts: replaces HA-automation-triggered webhooks with
  a background poller that detects per-slot remain_len drops and posts
  the same spool_usage payload an HA automation would have sent,
  reusing the existing lengthToWeight() conversion unchanged.
- lib/direct-printers.ts: printer config list stored in the existing
  Settings key/value table, no schema migration.
- lib/material-names.ts: material-code table (no ha_creality_ws to do
  this translation in direct mode).
- New /direct-printers page + nav link; small additive patches to
  api/printers/route.ts and api/settings/route.ts.
- docker-compose.direct.yml: runs the app alone, no HA container.
- DIRECT_MODE.md documents setup and, explicitly, what this does NOT
  confirm (no RFID auto-match without ha_creality_ws; per-slot usage-
  by-polling is new logic, not bench-verified against real hardware).

Verified before commit: tsc --noEmit clean throughout, a full
'next build' with system TLS certs succeeds, and vitest run passes
65/65 (57 original + 8 new for moonraker-direct.ts).

See DIRECT_MODE.md for full detail.
